WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.360 --> 00:00:07.549
One two three four.

00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:39.960
We call it blending.

00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:44.400
If you're blending right you can't pick out any individual voices but the soloist.

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:09.160
My name is Izzy Lloyd.

00:01:09.340 --> 00:01:12.800
I am a mechanical engineering and product design student at MIT

00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:15.200
and I'm an alto in the MIT Corallaries.

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:17.200
[singing]

00:01:32.380 --> 00:01:36.020
I joined Freshman Fall, so Fall of 2014.

00:01:36.020 --> 00:01:39.480
I am now the old crusty senior.

00:01:45.700 --> 00:01:50.120
These kinds of things are like truly the definition of like, "The whole is greater than the sum of the parts".

00:01:50.120 --> 00:01:52.120
[singing]

00:02:34.140 --> 00:02:35.180
Thank you all so much for coming out!

00:02:35.180 --> 00:02:38.920
We're the Corallaries of MIT, MIT's oldest co-ed acapella group.

00:02:39.040 --> 00:02:43.320
We invited you all to attend our concert tomorrow at 3:30 p.m. in Kresge Auditorium.

00:02:43.320 --> 00:02:45.320
[singing]

00:02:50.900 --> 00:02:55.920
This is a dedicated time where I just get to turn my brain off to engineering

00:02:55.980 --> 00:02:57.980
and turn it onto art.

00:03:09.480 --> 00:03:13.860
We are a very highly sought after group in terms of gigs.

00:03:13.880 --> 00:03:18.760
A of the times charity functions will have us, Institute events will have us a lot.

00:03:19.060 --> 00:03:24.200
And the money goes towards like recording albums, going on tour, competing in competitions.

00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:28.560
"We all get in formation for the next song while Caitlyn announces us..."

00:03:28.980 --> 00:03:31.720
It's hard when we step out of MIT.

00:03:32.800 --> 00:03:39.340
Because you've got all of these other brilliant acapella groups across the world

00:03:39.480 --> 00:03:44.820
who, the best ones, are made up of students who like, their major is music.

00:04:04.460 --> 00:04:07.180
Welcome to the Corallaries of MIT presenting "Game of Tones!"

00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:11.020
We are so excited to have you all here in great big Kresge Auditorium!

00:04:11.020 --> 00:04:13.940
[audience cheering]

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:16.220
[singing]

00:04:40.180 --> 00:04:45.180
Being able to step into this space where
we all create this beautiful thing together

00:04:45.540 --> 00:04:49.960
just like totally resets sort of the way I'm thinking and the way I'm feeling.

00:05:07.340 --> 00:05:09.340
[audience cheering]

